Original commit body from 57aa8439d306619e798050e58ad90900c17ac4d3:

Stage 2 of INV-midag, the same rule as #1176 (kotlin, scala, swift): the
enclosing declaration is found by its POSITION, via core `symbols_at` /
`symbol_declared_by`, never by its name.

- c: an `#ifdef`/`#else` pair defines one name twice in a file (tmux's
  compat/closefrom.c). CAnalyzer overrides `analyze()` and NEVER set
  `_current_file_symbols`, so `file_symbols()` fell back to the name-keyed
  dict. Once the lookup was by position, that dropped the other alternative's
  calls entirely; the fixture's reach assertion caught it. It is now set like
  the base loop. It was the only override of analyze() that skipped it.
- rust: already had a span index, built from `global_symbols`, which is keyed
  by QUALIFIED name. Three `impl From<_> for AardvarkError` blocks share
  `AardvarkError::from`, so two vanished from it. The index is now fed from
  the per-file list.
- ruby: a method defined twice (a reopened class; postal's
  MessageInspection#scan).
- csharp: one leaf name in two classes (livebook's ElixirKit.cs API.Stop /
  Release.Stop).
Each symbol span was checked to start at the node the walk reaches. Tests are
production-path and reach-first, and each was red on dev.

